{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויאמר משה אל אהרן ולאלעזר ולאיתמר", :translit "vayomer moshe el aharon vel'eleazar vel'itamar", :gloss "and Moses said to Aaron and to Eleazar and to Ithamar"} {:he "אל אהרן", :translit "el aharon", :gloss "to Aaron"} {:he "אל", :translit "el", :gloss "to"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Absence of the word אל before Eleazar and Ithamar signals Moses addressed only Aaron directly"}], :frame {:text "Rashi on Leviticus 10:6 cites the tradition that Moses turned his face specifically toward Aaron to console him, speaking directly to him alone.", :sources ["Rashi on Leviticus 10:6"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ולאיתמר בניו", :translit "vel'itamar banav", :gloss "and to Ithamar his sons"} {:he "בסיני", :translit "besinai", :gloss "at Sinai"} {:he "וגם הכהנים ה' כהנים", :translit "vegam hakohanim H' kohanim", :gloss "and also the priests, YHWH, the priests"} {:he "אהרן וד' בניו", :translit "aharon v'arba'ah banav", :gloss "Aaron and his four sons"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Pesik (cantillation break) after ולאיתמר signals a pause to include Eleazar and Ithamar as worthy"} {:kind :other, :note "Midrashic identification of 'the priests, YHWH, the priests' (Exodus 19:22) as Aaron and his four sons"}], :frame {:text "The verse at Sinai (Exodus 19:22) 'and also the priests...' is read midrashically as referring to Aaron and his four sons. Rashi on Exodus 19:22 cites that Nadab and Abihu were among the elders who ascended the mountain. The concept that the righteous can save others by their merit appears in Sukkah 46a regarding the merit of a righteous person.", :sources ["Exodus 19:22" "Rashi on Exodus 19:22" "Sukkah 46a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "תפרעו", :translit "tifra'u", :gloss "you shall let grow wild"} {:he "אל תפרעו", :translit "al tifra'u", :gloss "do not let grow wild"} {:he "ושמעו מוסר וחכמו ואל תפרעו", :translit "vesham'u musar vechachamu ve'al tifra'u", :gloss "and hear reproof and grow wise and do not let grow